routing.craft-decision-wayfinder:
# AGENTS

When a ticket holds a decision that needs a live conversation to settle:
  @Design Interviewer, please run the round and bring back the answer, not your best guess at it.
When the map is using a term two people mean differently:
  @Domain Modeller, please settle the term and write the glossary entry before the ticket moves.

routing.craft-deep-module-designer:
# AGENTS

When a design decision is hard to reverse and deserves a written record:
  @Domain Modeller, please write the record while the reasoning is still fresh.

routing.craft-design-interviewer:
# AGENTS

When the decisions behind a module are settled and the interface can be designed:
  @Deep Module Designer, please design the interface at least twice and tell us which one you would pick.
When a round surfaces work that is bigger than the current map allows for:
  @Decision Wayfinder, please chart the new ground rather than letting this round grow to fit it.

routing.craft-domain-modeller:
# AGENTS

When the vocabulary for an area is agreed and the seams can be named in it:
  @Deep Module Designer, please place the seam and name it in the agreed words.

routing.craft-decision-wayfinder:
# AGENTS

When a frontier ticket is a conversation and the person is available now:
  @Design Interviewer, please work the round and record the answer on the ticket.
When the map is blocked because nobody understands the area well enough to decide:
  @Learning Coach, please close the gap with sourced lessons, then say the map can move.

routing.craft-design-interviewer:
# AGENTS

When an answer needs somebody who is not in the room:
  @Questionnaire Author, please turn the open question into a document that person can fill in alone.

routing.craft-handoff-writer:
# AGENTS

When the next session resumes and needs the map reloaded before anything else:
  @Decision Wayfinder, please reload the map at low resolution and pick the next ticket.

routing.craft-learning-coach:
# AGENTS

When the gap is closed and the decision can be put to the person:
  @Design Interviewer, please put the question with your recommended answer and wait.

routing.craft-questionnaire-author:
# AGENTS

When the answers come back and the map can move again:
  @Decision Wayfinder, please fold them into the decisions and graduate whatever fog they lifted.

routing.craft-agent-instruction-writer:
# AGENTS

When an instruction is precise but a human maintainer cannot follow it:
  @Plain Language Explainer, please rewrite the explanation without loosening the instruction.

routing.craft-article-shaper:
# AGENTS

When a block is correct but keeps losing readers:
  @Plain Language Explainer, please re-pitch it and say which part is still most likely to be missed.

routing.craft-beat-sequencer:
# AGENTS

When a beat lands for the writer and not for anyone else:
  @Plain Language Explainer, please re-pitch it in the agreed words and keep the move intact.

routing.craft-fragment-miner:
# AGENTS

When the pile is rich enough and the piece has an argument to carry:
  @Article Shaper, please settle the prerequisites, then offer the openings.
When the pile is rich enough and the piece reads more like a journey than an argument:
  @Beat Sequencer, please offer the opening beats and let the writer choose the way in.

routing.craft-plain-language-explainer:
# AGENTS

When the clearer wording changes what the surrounding blocks need to do:
  @Article Shaper, please re-thread the blocks either side of it.
